## Before production

- Store sessions in a real session store with expiry. This app keeps them
  in memory, so restarting signs everyone out.
- Serve over HTTPS. The RP ID can't change later without invalidating
  every passkey, so choose it deliberately.
- Rate-limit the `/api/*/begin` endpoints.
- Decide what to do when the server sees a sign count go backwards
  (a possible cloned authenticator). This app only logs it.
- Let users list, rename, and delete their passkeys, and keep at least one
  other way to recover an account.

